.secrets/
.private-assets/
.venv/
.env
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
tests/.test-data/
tests/*.png
tests/*.html
tests/.*.json
tests/.*.zip

# Local run artifacts and generated deliverables, listed by tools/prepare_git.py. Git reads
# everything after a `#` on a pattern line as part of the pattern, so the reasons live here instead of
# beside the rules:
#   tests/.probe-data/       the database the browser test harness writes (tens of megabytes)
#   tests/.shutdown-data/    the database the shutdown test writes
#   tests/.shutdown-profile/ a browser profile left by the shutdown test
#   tests/shots/             pictures the checks produce for a human to look at
#   tests/*.log              logs from a locally started server
#   tests/.*-profile/        browser profiles from the test harness
#   deliverables/*           the keepsake picture and its stroke sidecar: produced from the event's
#                            data by tools/export_wall_sheet.py, and the sidecar holds personal data
tests/.probe-data/
tests/.release-probe-data*/
tests/.shutdown-data/
tests/.shutdown-profile/
tests/shots/
tests/*.log
tests/.*-profile/
deliverables/*
backups/
.coverage
htmlcov/
# Scratch files, such as the message a commit is written from: `git add -A` picks them up before they
# are deleted, which left one in the index once.
*.tmp
